{:edb/db-before-t 1177 :edb/db-after-t 1178 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534490 50 #inst "2026-10-07T08:39:20.176Z" 13194139534490 true] [17592186096358 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/assets/bf61fd6b36dd17d2c9f6d6f570a8bad9111d10da11df8f69e39069d7fb4478cf.png)\n\nFind the area bounded between the curve ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/assets/8cdef67ff9afa667ed298cc0bb29e1727cfd7208fca347fb2b0ae253a1abdebf.png) the ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/assets/0389cce819c15d700c69e6ade974bd826bb0524b355de895a27e69589ad0afd5.png)-axis, and the lines ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/assets/81356f9909beb212c6d1c0dd7d3792dfacae911b236f1c8fa22ff0d3a508544e.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/assets/32dbbb5be19c5504a2aa53d2f92b5df909a2417272b8c3e1d6c6f0c9f350b1d9.png) as shown above." 13194139534490 true] [17592186096358 1100 "Find the area bounded between the curve $x=y^2-2y+2$, the $y$-axis, and the lines $y=1$ and $y=2$, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1041/Source/Images/ba7fd1150e24e1bce909556ef88947a8.png)" 13194139534490 false] [17592186096358 1145 "To find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/assets/3a73881568cbe0c10ae1e24446a47a522072eb67093c9d5fd34ca0862e02be7a.png)\n\nSince the region lies to the left of the ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/assets/4cf2e90080f1ae459e72ac253d6617d0defdcc3be58a1ca385bddc3215034eca.png)-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/assets/321fc255901c5f86d2c324df57b60faa428e5cbdd2cba412f643cff6df19422e.png)" 13194139534490 true] [17592186096358 1145 "To find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA &= ∫_{c}^{d}x(y)dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{1}^{2}(y^{2} - 2y + 2)dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{1}^{2}y^{2}dy - 2∫_{1}^{2}ydy + ∫_{1}^{2}2dy \\\\\n&= \\frac{y^{3}}{3}\\begin{vmatrix}_{1}^{2} - 2 \\cdot \\frac{y^{2}}{2} & _{1}^{2} + 2y\\end{vmatrix}_{1}^{2} \\\\\n&= (\\frac{8}{3} - \\frac{1}{3}) - (4 - 1) + (4 - 2) \\\\\n&= \\frac{7}{3} - 3 + 2 \\\\\n&= \\frac{4}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534490 false] [17592186096359 1145 "First, we find the $y$-intercepts of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny^{2} - 4 &= 0 \\\\\ny^{2} &= 4 \\\\\ny &= ± 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we draw a sketch of the region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1041/Source/Images/0a73f14099d8a6940e2ee8a6785c25e2.png)\n\nWe want the area between the curve $x=y^2-4$ and the $y$-axis from $y=-2$ to $y=2$. To find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA &= ∫_{c}^{d}x(y)dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{-2}^{2}(y^{2} - 4)dy \\\\\n&= 2∫_{0}^{2}(y^{2} - 4)dy \\\\\n&= 2∫_{0}^{2}y^{2}dy - 8∫_{0}^{2}dy \\\\\n&= 2 \\cdot \\frac{y^{3}}{3} \\mid _{0}^{2} - 8y \\mid _{0}^{2} \\\\\n&= 2(\\frac{8}{3} - 0) - 8(2 - 0) \\\\\n&= \\frac{16}{3} - 16 \\\\\n&=-\\frac{32}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe obtained a negative number because the region lies to the left of the $y$-axis. So the area that we want is\n\n$$\n\\left|-\\dfrac{32}{3}\\right| = \\dfrac{32}{3}\n$$" 13194139534490 false] [17592186096359 1145 "First, we find the $y$-intercepts of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-4 & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4 \\\\ y & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we draw a sketch of the region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/assets/f2a29faeb9db8e622a21a0e77bea911960a5c64d87a2c900ecd0c0213b2e4bce.png)\n\nWe want the area between the curve $x=y^2-4$ and the $y$-axis from  $y=-2$ to $y=2.$ To find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}({y}^{2}-4)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{2}({y}^{2}-4)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y-8{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\cdot {\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{2}-8y{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =2(\\frac{8}{3}-0)-8(2-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}-16 \\\\  & =-\\frac{32}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe obtained a negative number because the region lies to the left of the $y$-axis. So the area that we want is $\\left|-\\dfrac{32}{3}\\right| = \\dfrac{32}{3}.$" 13194139534490 true] [17592186096476 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/assets/eb7118486df97c3abae6c8492170090df0c654064799e04826a39a94bcfa22a8.png)\n\nFind the area between the curve $y=\\sqrt{x+1},$ the $y$-axis, and the lines $y=0$ and $y=1,$ as shown above." 13194139534490 true] [17592186096476 1100 "Find the area between the curve $y=\\sqrt{x+1}$, the $y$-axis, and the lines $y=0$ and $y=1$, as shown above.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1041/Source/Images/8eb4608fe3ade4f8a475b24df1952eb2.png)" 13194139534490 false] [17592186096476 1145 "First, we make $x$ the subject:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny &= \\sqrt{x + 1} \\\\\ny^{2} &= x + 1 \\\\\nx &= y^{2} - 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA &= ∫_{0}^{1}(y^{2} - 1)dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}y^{2}dy - ∫_{0}^{1}dy \\\\\n&= \\frac{y^{3}}{3} \\mid _{0}^{1} - y \\mid _{0}^{1} \\\\\n&= (\\frac{1}{3} - 0) - (1 - 0) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3} - 1 \\\\\n&=-\\frac{2}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe obtained a negative number because the region lies to the left of the $y$-axis. So the area that we want is\n\n$$\n\\left|-\\dfrac{2}{3}\\right| = \\dfrac{2}{3}\n$$" 13194139534490 false] [17592186096476 1145 "First, we make $x$ the subject:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\sqrt{x+1} \\\\ {y}^{2} & =x+1 \\\\ x & ={y}^{2}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({y}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y-{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{1}-y{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{3}-0)-(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}-1 \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe obtained a negative number because the region lies to the left of the $y$-axis. So the area that we want is $\\left|-\\dfrac{2}{3}\\right| = \\dfrac{2}{3}.$" 13194139534490 true] [17592186096559 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291636 13194139534490 true] [17592186096559 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291643 13194139534490 true] [17592186096559 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291650 13194139534490 true] [17592186096559 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291664 13194139534490 true] [17592186096559 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291671 13194139534490 true] [17592186096560 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291657 13194139534490 true] [17592186096560 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291675 13194139534490 true] [17592186096560 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291678 13194139534490 true] [17592186096560 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291684 13194139534490 true] [17592186096560 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291691 13194139534490 true] [17592186096671 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291667 13194139534490 true] [17592186096671 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291681 13194139534490 true] [17592186096671 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291698 13194139534490 true] [17592186096671 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291705 13194139534490 true] [17592186096671 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291712 13194139534490 true] [17592186291636 1017 #edb/ref 17592186291637 13194139534490 true] [17592186291636 1089 "q-10025" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291636 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534490 true] [17592186291636 1100 "Find the area bounded between the curve $x=(y-1)^{2},$ the $y$-axis, and the lines $y=0$ and $y=1.$" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291636 1113 #uuid "75d55022-cb9d-5432-9fd1-819a6f8b9ed5" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291636 1145 "To find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(y-1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({y}^{2}-2y+1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y-2{\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{1}-2\\cdot {\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}|}_{0}^{1}+y{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{3}-0)-2(\\frac{1}{2}-0)+(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}-1+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291637 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291638 13194139534490 true] [17592186291637 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291639 13194139534490 true] [17592186291637 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291640 13194139534490 true] [17592186291637 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291641 13194139534490 true] [17592186291637 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291642 13194139534490 true] [17592186291637 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534490 true] [17592186291637 1041 "selection" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291637 1104 #edb/ref 17592186291642 13194139534490 true] [17592186291637 1110 #uuid "b104aaac-56fb-5c7c-9daf-29558dbbb6c7" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291638 1034 "-\\frac{2}{3}" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291638 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534490 true] [17592186291638 1111 #uuid "2219b6e2-40d8-5c76-ac5d-539ceaa15ee3" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291639 1034 "\\frac{2}{3}" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291639 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534490 true] [17592186291639 1111 #uuid "14492073-82d7-5105-a679-c74ee65cda5c" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291640 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291640 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534490 true] [17592186291640 1111 #uuid "595bdb6c-0750-51fe-9360-02380d4bc75a" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291641 1034 "\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139534490 tr