}_{0}^{1}{y}^{5}\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-{\\frac{{y}^{6}}{6}|}_{0}^{1}+y{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-(\\frac{1}{6}-0)+(1-0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{6}+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291651 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291652 13194139534490 true] [17592186291651 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291653 13194139534490 true] [17592186291651 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291654 13194139534490 true] [17592186291651 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291655 13194139534490 true] [17592186291651 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291656 13194139534490 true] [17592186291651 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534490 true] [17592186291651 1041 "selection" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291651 1104 #edb/ref 17592186291652 13194139534490 true] [17592186291651 1110 #uuid "50b12b50-5c6f-5d6e-b352-36bd560b3ab5" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291652 1034 "\\frac{5}{6}" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291652 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534490 true] [17592186291652 1111 #uuid "689c0d6a-56c7-5f86-8fcc-5bc659e66828" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291653 1034 "\\frac{8}{3}" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291653 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534490 true] [17592186291653 1111 #uuid "183ed92d-e8d5-5b44-a3c6-efc9c16f27df" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291654 1034 "\\frac{19}{6}" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291654 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534490 true] [17592186291654 1111 #uuid "19dd979b-934b-5418-95f0-f8c3b8a8f1de" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291655 1034 "\\frac{1}{6}" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291655 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534490 true] [17592186291655 1111 #uuid "37e96874-f1e1-5f0b-abcd-ecaa735bb651" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291656 1034 "-\\frac{11}{4}" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291656 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534490 true] [17592186291656 1111 #uuid "1b39812c-56ae-51ca-9d2a-4325a928755e" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291657 1017 #edb/ref 17592186291658 13194139534490 true] [17592186291657 1089 "q-117485" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291657 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534490 true] [17592186291657 1100 "Find the area of the finite region bounded between the curve $x=9y-{y}^{3}$ and the $y$-axis for $y\\ge 0.$" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291657 1113 #uuid "9ef13261-2249-54c7-9c1e-84f17b27b72d" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291657 1145 "First, we find the $y$-intercepts of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9y-{y}^{3} & =0 \\\\ y(9-{y}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ y & =0,\\pm 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we draw a sketch of the region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/assets/bbcf218e7b6181c861ba4c804357cc53ae6004453914259a9fe98ad5f09ac4d4.png)\n\nWe want to find the area between the curve $x=9y-{y}^{3}$ and the $y$-axis from  $y=0$ to $y=3.$ \nTo find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(9y-{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =9{\\int }_{0}^{3}y\\,\\text{d}y-{\\int }_{0}^{3}{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =9\\cdot {\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}|}_{0}^{3}-{\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =9\\cdot (\\frac{(3)^{2}}{2}-0)-(\\frac{(3)^{4}}{4}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{81}{2}-\\frac{81}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{81}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291658 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291659 13194139534490 true] [17592186291658 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291660 13194139534490 true] [17592186291658 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291661 13194139534490 true] [17592186291658 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291662 13194139534490 true] [17592186291658 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291663 13194139534490 true] [17592186291658 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534490 true] [17592186291658 1041 "selection" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291658 1104 #edb/ref 17592186291661 13194139534490 true] [17592186291658 1110 #uuid "8572001a-818f-5e75-b818-8c8fa08fb31f" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291659 1034 "\\frac{9}{2}" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291659 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534490 true] [17592186291659 1111 #uuid "ca032f50-1f40-54cf-9f46-d43796ab9f5e" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291660 1034 "\\frac{27}{2}" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291660 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534490 true] [17592186291660 1111 #uuid "eb2f0628-8c1c-530d-bdfd-8bb434e1c508" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291661 1034 "\\frac{81}{4}" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291661 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534490 true] [17592186291661 1111 #uuid "078800a8-cebe-58ce-9e17-9d758f699b69" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291662 1034 "27" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291662 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534490 true] [17592186291662 1111 #uuid "e34ea8be-25d3-5c8c-a9a0-ed09df3c7ea0" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291663 1034 "\\frac{81}{2}" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291663 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534490 true] [17592186291663 1111 #uuid "099d7abf-4a6c-53db-80d8-643b859ec24e" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291664 1017 #edb/ref 17592186291665 13194139534490 true] [17592186291664 1089 "q-316692" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291664 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534490 true] [17592186291664 1100 "Find the area $A$ bounded between the curve $x=2-{y}^{8}$, the $y$-axis, and the lines $y=0$ and $y=1.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291664 1113 #uuid "dd45aa8e-4c97-5744-93f5-74fc6336bf9d" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291664 1145 "To find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(2-{y}^{8})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y\\,-\\,{\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{8}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\cdot y{|}_{0}^{1}\\,-\\,{\\frac{{y}^{9}}{9}|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =2(1-0)\\,-\\,(\\frac{1}{9}-0) \\\\  & =2-\\frac{1}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291665 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291666 13194139534490 true] [17592186291665 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534490 true] [17592186291665 1041 "field-1" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291665 1104 #edb/ref 17592186291666 13194139534490 true] [17592186291665 1110 #uuid "ee4e3867-8189-55ef-88a1-130c87e558ff" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291666 1034 "\\frac{17}{9}" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291666 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534490 true] [17592186291666 1111 #uuid "efe38760-1391-5db3-8899-e8200bb8be21" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291667 1017 #edb/ref 17592186291668 13194139534490 true] [17592186291667 1089 "q-316744" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291667 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534490 true] [17592186291667 1100 "Find the area $A$ between the curve $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)$, the $y$-axis, and the lines $y=0$ and $y=2.$\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}} ." 13194139534490 true] [17592186291667 1113 #uuid "a144a16a-629d-56f3-8574-ea0e972aadca" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291667 1145 "First, we make $x$ the subject:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x) \\\\ {e}^{y} & =3x \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{y}\\,dy \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{y}\\,dy \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\,{e}^{y}{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}({e}^{2}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}({e}^{2}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291668 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291669 13194139534490 true] [17592186291668 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291670 13194139534490 true] [17592186291668 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534490 true] [17592186291668 1041 "field-1" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291668 1104 #edb/ref 17592186291669 13194139534490 true] [17592186291668 1110 #uuid "0e63584e-aa9b-5412-afa2-f9536d28d011" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291669 1034 "\\frac{e^2-1}{3}" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291669 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534490 true] [17592186291669 1111 #uuid "c9dd518e-7bce-5448-896b-5c2afe49512d" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291670 1034 "0" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291670 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534490 true] [17592186291670 1111 #uuid "53ba15e0-d532-514c-ad3f-87da629b06d1" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291671 1017 #edb/ref 17592186291672 13194139534490 true] [17592186291671 1089 "q-346471" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291671 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534490 true] [17592186291671 1100 "Find the area $A$ bounded between the curve $x=24-6{y}^{2}$, the $y$-axis, and the lines $y=-3$ and $y=-2.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291671 1113 #uuid "8f330b06-b851-5eea-b5ae-a44580d18fff" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291671 1145 "To find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3}^{-2}(24-6{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =24{\\int }_{-3}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,-\\,6{\\int }_{-3}^{-2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =24y\\,{|}_{-3}^{-2}-2{y}^{3}\\,{|}_{-3}^{-2} \\\\  & =24(-2-(-3))-2(-8-(-27)) \\\\  & =24-38 \\\\  & =-14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies to the left of the $y$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $|-14|=14.$" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291672 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291673 13194139534490 true] [17592186291672 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291674 13194139534490 true] [17592186291672 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534490 true] [17592186291672 1041 "field-1" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291672 1104 #edb/ref 17592186291674 13194139534490 true] [17592186291672 1110 #uuid "1501ff89-eff9-5744-be01-0ee981643584" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291673 1034 "-14" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291673 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534490 true] [17592186291673 1111 #uuid "2a652438-f095-564f-a5d6-4cfe65cd3591" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291674 1034 "14" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291674 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534490 true] [17592186291674 1111 #uuid "1529412f-d822-5d09-b7ec-05a00d809fb1" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291675 1017 #edb/ref 17592186291676 13194139534490 true] [17592186291675 1089 "q-346643" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291675 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534490 true] [17592186291675 1100 "Find the area $A$ of the closed region between the curve $x=\\frac{3}{8}{y}^{2}-6$ and the $y$-axis. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291675 1113 #uuid "70f526a6-c520-5a75-9821-854064664a16" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291675 1145 "First, we find the $y$-intercepts of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{8}{y}^{2}-6 & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3}{8}{y}^{2} & =6 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =16 \\\\ y & =\\pm 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we draw a sketch of the region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/assets/c5cd702bed84fd0ffc7f0e3a9510bdb3411bb8f77424786f9445c4d559392416.png)\n\nWe want the area between the curve $x=\\frac{3}{8}{y}^{2}-6$ and the $y$-axis from $y=-4$ to $y=4.$\nTo find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{-4}^{4}(\\frac{3}{8}{y}^{2}-6)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}{\\int }_{-4}^{4}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y-6{\\int }_{-4}^{4}\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}{y}^{3}\\,{|}_{-4}^{4}-6y\\,{|}_{-4}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}(64-(-64))-6(4-(-4)) \\\\  & =16-48 \\\\  & =-32\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe obtained a negative number because the region lies to the left of the $y$-axis. So, the area that we want is $|-32|=32.$" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291676 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291677 13194139534490 true] [17592186291676 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534490 true] [17592186291676 1041 "field-1" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291676 1104 #edb/ref 17592186291677 13194139534490 true] [17592186291676 1110 #uuid "f9912f89-2a76-5c6f-83f2-37e089f26131" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291677 1034 "32" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291677 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534490 true] [17592186291677 1111 #uuid "59dd3b77-b659-5b2d-a0a1-a0baf49d3e79" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291678 1017 #edb/ref 17592186291679 13194139534490 true] [17592186291678 1089 "q-346702" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291678 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534490 true] [17592186291678 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/assets/7808295803d04d2c996ca7d36110f070a60f4491107ad1c831e6fa8ea9f85678.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the finite region bounded between the curve $x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi y)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi y)$ and the $y$-axis, as shown above.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291678 1113 #uuid "eeb02085-ddb1-57a7-8b02-f5a5cea62d5f" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291678 1145 "First, we find the $y$-intercepts of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi y)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi y) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi y) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi y) \\\\ \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi y)}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi y)} & =1 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\pi y) & =1 \\\\ \\pi y & =…,-\\frac{3\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{5\\pi }{4},… \\\\ y & =…,-\\frac{3}{4},\\frac{1}{4},\\frac{5}{4},…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that we want to find the area between the curve $x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi y)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi y)$ and the $y$-axis from $y=-\\frac{3}{4}$ to $y=\\frac{1}{4}.$ To find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3/4}^{1/4}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi y)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi y))\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3/4}^{1/4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi y)\\,\\text{d}y-{\\int }_{-3/4}^{1/4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi y)}{\\pi }|}_{-3/4}^{1/4}-{\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi y)}{\\pi }|}_{-3/4}^{1/4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\pi }[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\frac{3\\pi }{4})]-\\frac{1}{\\pi }[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{3\\pi }{4})] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\pi }[\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})]-\\frac{1}{\\pi }[\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})] \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\pi }-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\pi } \\\\  & =-\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{\\pi }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe obtained a negative number because the region lies to the left of the $y$-axis. So the area that we want is\n\n$$\nA=|-\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{\\pi }|=\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{\\pi }.\n$$" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291679 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291680 13194139534490 true] [17592186291679 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534490 true] [17592186291679 1041 "field-1" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291679 1104 #edb/ref 17592186291680 13194139534490 true] [17592186291679 1110 #uuid "e2a37ff8-cbdb-503d-a02a-8329ecaf2f00" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291680 1034 "\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{\\pi}" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291680 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534490 true] [17592186291680 1111 #uuid "bad2e130-3b94-5e88-8611-354ddf60b7b9" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291681 1017 #edb/ref 17592186291682 13194139534490 true] [17592186291681 1089 "q-346744" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291681 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534490 true] [17592186291681 1100 "Find the area $A$ between the curve $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)$, the $y$-axis, and the lines $y=0$ and $y=1.$\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291681 1113 #uuid "64e2114f-4471-5a1f-a135-f05bbf0c184c" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291681 1145 "First, we make $x$ the subject:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1) \\\\ {e}^{y} & =x+1 \\\\ x & ={e}^{y}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({e}^{y}-1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y-{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={e}^{y}\\,{|}_{0}^{1}-y\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(e-1)-(1-0) \\\\  & =e-1-1 \\\\  & =e-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291682 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291683 13194139534490 true] [17592186291682 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534490 true] [17592186291682 1041 "field-1" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291682 1104 #edb/ref 17592186291683 13194139534490 true] [17592186291682 1110 #uuid "4e3fc26e-9d8f-512f-ab0d-f82347cf8192" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291683 1034 "e-2" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291683 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534490 true] [17592186291683 1111 #uuid "fcfce802-f1d6-547c-a44e-3c8022e8b988" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291684 1017 #edb/ref 17592186291685 13194139534490 true] [17592186291684 1089 "q-78886" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291684 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534490 true] [17592186291684 1100 "Find the area of the finite region bounded between the curve $x=2{y}^{2}-2$ and the $y$-axis." 13194139534490 true] [17592186291684 1113 #uuid "cbe96f44-91be-573a-850a-cb103d394f5c" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291684 1145 "First, we find the $y$-intercepts of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{y}^{2}-2 & =0 \\\\ 2{y}^{2} & =2 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =1 \\\\ y & =\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we draw a sketch of the region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/assets/a2156d559a715d668f064c91132719d2678ab4af66bf83591fa5687d6e23d95e.png)\n\nWe want to find the area between the curve $x=2{y}^{2}-2$ and the $y$-axis from $y=-1$ to $y=1.$ \nTo find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}(2{y}^{2}-2)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2{y}^{2}-2)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y-4{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =4\\cdot {\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{1}-4\\cdot y{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =4(\\frac{1}{3}-0)-4(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}-4 \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe obtained a negative number because the region lies to the left of the $y$-axis. So the area that we want is $|-\\frac{8}{3}|=\\frac{8}{3}.$" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291685 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291686 13194139534490 true] [17592186291685 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291687 13194139534490 true] [17592186291685 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291688 13194139534490 true] [17592186291685 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291689 13194139534490 true] [17592186291685 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291690 13194139534490 true] [17592186291685 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534490 true] [17592186291685 1041 "selection" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291685 1104 #edb/ref 17592186291689 13194139534490 true] [17592186291685 1110 #uuid "69cc6c78-dd62-5ed9-9b65-9ee5f9e90397" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291686 1034 "\\frac{7}{2}" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291686 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534490 true] [17592186291686 1111 #uuid "f1a7b660-ed53-5db3-a2da-e1edfe934c65" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291687 1034 "\\frac{16}{3}" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291687 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534490 true] [17592186291687 1111 #uuid "2e9b153b-6b8b-5440-9369-27ce7ca2f8e3" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291688 1034 "\\frac{5}{2}" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291688 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534490 true] [17592186291688 1111 #uuid "71daee3c-fe18-5e49-ba74-1b1609fde443" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291689 1034 "\\frac{8}{3}" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291689 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534490 true] [17592186291689 1111 #uuid "ab5d5ca1-7ded-5dee-8fb5-16b4d72b5509" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291690 1034 "\\frac{4}{3}" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291690 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534490 true] [17592186291690 1111 #uuid "8eca0171-0492-563d-9631-de66c243db3b" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291691 1017 #edb/ref 17592186291692 13194139534490 true] [17592186291691 1089 "q-78892" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291691 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534490 true] [17592186291691 1100 "Find the area of the finite region bounded between the curve $x=2-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}$ and the $y$-axis." 13194139534490 true] [17592186291691 1113 #uuid "742f1c9a-b044-582d-a39f-35ae12f44185" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291691 1145 "First, we find the $y$-intercepts of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2} & =2 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4 \\\\ y & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we draw a sketch of the region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/assets/5e3f9d31bc4cb5687d784097679861644cc55ce667ea1469d0d790bfe879706f.png)\n\nWe want to find the area between the curve $x=2-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}$ and the $y$-axis from $y=-2$ to $y=2.$ \nTo find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}(2-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{2}(2-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y-{\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =4\\cdot y{|}_{0}^{2}-{\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =4(2-0)-(\\frac{(2)^{3}}{3}-0) \\\\  & =8-\\frac{8}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291692 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291693 13194139534490 true] [17592186291692 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291694 13194139534490 true] [17592186291692 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291695 13194139534490 true] [17592186291692 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291696 13194139534490 true] [17592186291692 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291697 13194139534490 true] [17592186291692 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534490 true] [17592186291692 1041 "selection" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291692 1104 #edb/ref 17592186291694 13194139534490 true] [17592186291692 1110 #uuid "097bb06c-d77b-59ef-b8c3-4559e6743ecb" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291693 1034 "\\frac{64}{3}" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291693 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534490 true] [17592186291693 1111 #uuid "4b74a38b-cecd-5d98-af5c-20121856ae89" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291694 1034 "\\frac{16}{3}" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291694 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534490 true] [17592186291694 1111 #uuid "2cc0b4e6-ed25-5395-9ca5-326cd8d81821" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291695 1034 "\\frac{32}{3}" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291695 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534490 true] [17592186291695 1111 #uuid "96ac1c1c-9d7d-56f8-b9a0-76839093b269" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291696 1034 "\\frac{8}{3}" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291696 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534490 true] [17592186291696 1111 #uuid "8b3d4b51-d9c4-5a16-9773-10c2ae8fe132" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291697 1034 "\\frac{4}{3}" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291697 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534490 true] [17592186291697 1111 #uuid "2df12cbf-235a-5860-8134-e6c1a5e9db34" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291698 1017 #edb/ref 17592186291699 13194139534490 true] [17592186291698 1089 "q-78896" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291698 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534490 true] [17592186291698 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013903/assets/446dddc9ec5393005b5aa9fff9d45760c6f2e80da97fd459cdd74cf4f8575f71.png)\n\nFind the area bounded between the curve $y=\\sqrt[3]{x-1}+1,$ the $y$-axis and the lines $y=0$ and $y=1,$ as shown above." 13194139534490 true] [17592186291698 1113 #uuid "de6ca82c-874b-5d47-8c60-3c70fc49188e" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291698 1145 "First, we make $x$ the subject:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\sqrt[3]{x-1}+1 \\\\ y-1 & =\\sqrt[3]{x-1} \\\\ (y-1)^{3} & =x-1 \\\\ x & =(y-1)^{3}+1 \\\\ x & ={y}^{3}-3{y}^{2}+3y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({y}^{3}-3{y}^{2}+3y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y-3{\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y+3{\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}|}_{0}^{1}-3\\cdot {\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{1}+3\\cdot {\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{4}-0)-3(\\frac{1}{3}-0)+3(\\frac{1}{2}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}-1+\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291699 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291700 13194139534490 true] [17592186291699 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291701 13194139534490 true] [17592186291699 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291702 13194139534490 true] [17592186291699 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291703 13194139534490 true] [17592186291699 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291704 13194139534490 true] [17592186291699 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534490 true] [17592186291699 1041 "selection" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291699 1104 #edb/ref 17592186291703 13194139534490 true] [17592186291699 1110 #uuid "26b7bbc3-2473-559b-96e6-caa1992f1303" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291700 1034 "\\frac{5}{2}" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291700 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534490 true] [17592186291700 1111 #uuid "c6a9ae96-5722-51b5-9dea-72539452f983" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291701 1034 "\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291701 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534490 true] [17592186291701 1111 #uuid "e6fe71fb-5ffb-5f7c-97a7-bdeaee93de30" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291702 1034 "1" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291702 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534490 true] [17592186291702 1111 #uuid "64142ebd-f4d5-5abd-b930-93e75013addf" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291703 1034 "\\frac{3}{4}" 13194139534490 true] [17592186291703 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534490 true] [1759218